ter asking her about romulus being a  king marcus takes it from her and he  wears it and then they discover another  one of those giant dodecahedrons a  pentagonal temple which is probably  really exciting for marcus because  you'll remember in the first season  that's where he first heard saul's voice  talk to him it's also where he became  the leader after the temple burned his  rival this temple isn't completely  intact it's damaged in a way that  they're able to enter it and inside it  they find a pit above that there's a  smaller dodecahedron on a chain that is  made to lower someone into it justina  inspects it and says there's a trial  that has to be passed she can't read all  the markings but can recognize the tree  of knowledge after decima eggs him on  marcus gets into the chair and they  start to lower him eventually he reaches  the bottom of the chain there's a big  serpent skeleton below where it stopped  that collapses when he crosses over it  to enter this tunnel that is actually  blocked by bones so he starts to clear  them back up on the surface it's raining  which i think this is the first time  we've ever seen that happen and i guess  this means it isn't acidic enough to  burn everyone up the mithraic faithful  are using their down time to get a  prayer circle going and then varial  returns to start picking them off with  ruthless efficiency she eliminates them  one by one and marcus gets the idea that  something might be going wrong on the  surface when justina goes screaming by  on her way to the bottom of the pit he's  on the mission so he continues digging  and varell continues slaughtering his  followers this was a pretty entertaining  sequence all the way around but i  thought her stabbing the kid with the  eye patch and his good eye was a  particularly nice touch when marcus  finally pushes his way through the  passage he finds a being slumped against  the wall it resembles what they  described as the devolved human that  tried to attack mother in the season 1  finale it's sort of wrapped in snake  skin and is carrying an intact metal  card that marcus pockets it opens its  eyes when he touches it and then  romulus's tooth starts to glow in  response to that i'd be lying if i said  the mechanics of what's happening here  all make sense in the moment but when it  starts making noises marcus tears it off  of his neck and throws it on the floor  it releases what looks like a gas that  makes its way over to the creature and  when it inhales it it transforms into  one of the creatures we saw coming out  of the pits in season one after a brief  struggle marcus shoots it and then sees  that his ride is taking off the chair is  going back up but he is able to leap and  climb inside as it's ascending  decima makes a break for it she's going  for the tank she totally leaves holly  behind and when she gets there she  thinks she's escaped but actually virile  is already inside there too there's a  brief moment where decima thinks she  might be able to talk her way out of  what happened but her android is talking  literally when she says she wants her to  understand what it's like to get your  face cut off after she does that she  drags her body back to the pit and hangs  it up and it's the first thing marcus  encounters when he gets back to the  surface he's reunited with holly who is  the only survivor but while they're  burning the dead bodies father and  lucius arrived to bring her home lucius  is fairly upset that father won't let  him kill marcus on the spot but holly  had jumped in the way she's right there  she's freaking out that he's really the  prophet so they end up just taking him  prisoner although father does say that  he'll keep his promise to let lucius do  what he wants with him the leeches were  effective in saving paul from becoming a  snake it appears that he's making a full  recovery but who knows if there will be  any lingering effects he's delighted to  learn that sue got the idea when she  prayed again she explains that she  thinks the voice is something alien  rather than a god but he doesn't believe  that for a second it was soul as far as  he's concerned all of this seems to work  to help him put his animosity towards  her aside and i suppose they'll both  learn soon that marcus has been captured  sue is still on the hook to the voice  though and the episode ends with it  telling her to grow the seeds which is  referring to the box that paul found  that is now presumably somewhere in the  tarantula she says i'll do anything you  want just keep him safe as it cuts to  black so wow virile really thinned out  the cast in her quest for revenge i was  really surprised that they killed off so  many people especially decima and  tamerlane since they were just  introduced as new characters not many  misreacts left at this point either  although there were three victims that  went into the pit so who knows there  might be something going on there in the  beginning of the season it was all about  number seven is he going to be a threat  then we had this ancient android but it  was virile that really racked up a body  count hard to say how campion's gonna  react to that he was definitely feeling  her and hey she's still out there her  story is not over it's almost comical  now when i think back to the  anticipation i had of marcus finding  some major clue at the bottom of the pit  i figured he would find another mural or  something along those lines but nope  just another creature who is i don't  know allergic to ancient earth teeth  such a weird little trip into the pit  there although i gotta say him seeing  the body come flying by as he's clearing  the bone wall was a pretty awesome setup  also i did watch the episode extra for  this one where the showrunner gave some  more information about what was  happening there he says this creature is  somewhere between a human and one of the  other creatures the ones we saw  scurrying around on all fours it's  something that didn't allow itself to  devolve all the way then he said that  the tooth kind of disintegrated into  these little nanobots and then suddenly  this creature starts to devolve it made  for a crazy episode and got me a lot  more hyped up for the ones that are  still left i suppose the card that  marcus took from him that's going to  turn out to be important and since he's  been taken prisoner that's probably  going to get confiscated either way now  that sue is working for the voice he's  got somebody on the inside and i'm sure  that box is gonna get opened and we're  gonna find out what's going on there so  things are looking pretty good like i  said i thought that we would learn a  little bit more about father's android  we're still just kind of getting the  tease there and really number seven has  been on the bench for the last two  episodes so hopefully we'll get some  movement with him as well mother and  father's conversation kind of pointed  out how things have strayed away from  the primary focus of course she's making  moves to protect her children like  shutting down the trust but all of that  is made more complicated by number  seven's existence which they're keeping  a secret as to how she's connected plus  they still haven't explained what they  learned about the planet and just in  general there is a lot of situations  where people aren't telling the whole  truth father does seem to be pretty  absorbed in his project and how could he  not be hopefully it'll start talking or  communicating soon the projection of  tempus baby felt like it might be  protective to humans to me not sure what  everyone else thinks about that that  baby is coming and that seems like it'll  probably be important and i think that  would be a good place to leave things so  a lot to look forward to let me know in  the comments what you're thinking about  what you thought about this episode what  you're hoping to see for the rest of the  season please like this video if you  enjoyed it please subscribe to my  channel if you haven't already and  thanks for watching i'll talk to you  soon


